2 CONT
2 CONT Gouverneur intérimaire de la Nouvelle-France le 6-5-au 12-9-1665, 
2 CONT
2 CONT gouverneur le 7-11-1645 au 2-9-1648, 9-9-1649 au 21-8-1651, 8-9-1652 au 16-7-1653 et juillet 1658 à 1662 Trois-Rivières 
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCE: Genéalogie du Québec
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacques Leneuf-Delapoterie was a fur trader, co-founder of the Communaute des Habitants 1645, interim Governor of New France May 6, 1665 to September 12, 1665, Governor November 7, 1645 to September 2, 1648, September 9, 1649 to  
2 CONC August 21, 1651, September 8, 1652 to July 16, 1653, and July 1658 to 1662 at Trois Rivieres; concession of the Seigneurie of Portneuf (or LaPoterie) April 16, 1647, ceded to Rene Robineau July 7, 1671; concession of the fief of L
2 CONC aPoterie (or Niverville) at Trois Rivieres April 7, 1660, sold to Pierre Boucher after July 5, 1668: concession of the Seigneurie of the Ile aux Cochons near Trois Rivieres March 29, 1649, made into a noble fief April 7, 1660.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Cofondateur de la Communauté des Habitants en 1645.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gouverneur intérimaire de la Nouvelle-France le 6-5-au 12-9-1665,
2 CONT
2 CONT gouverneur le 7-11-1645 au 2-9-1648, 9-9-1649 au 21-8-1651, 8-9-1652 au 16-7-1653 et juillet 1658 à 1662 Trois-Rivières
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCE: Genéalogie du Québec
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacques Leneuf-Delapoterie was a fur trader, co-founder of the Communaute des Habitants 1645, interim Governor of New France May 6, 1665 to September 12, 1665, Governor November 7, 1645 to September 2, 1648, September 9, 1649 to A
2 CONC ugust 21, 1651, September 8, 1652 to July 16, 1653, and July 1658 to 1662 at Trois Rivieres; concession of the Seigneurie of Portneuf (or LaPoterie) April 16, 1647, ceded to Rene Robineau July 7, 1671; concession of the fief of La
2 CONC Poterie (or Niverville) at Trois Rivieres April 7, 1660, sold to Pierre Boucher after July 5, 1668: concession of the Seigneurie of the Ile aux Cochons near Trois Rivieres March 29, 1649, made into a noble fief April 7, 1660.
