1 NOTE Married 1630 Marie-Marguerite LeGardeur at Thury-Harcourt, Normandie, France; sources: family (3 children) is listed in Jette pg 713-714;  Drouin pg 834; <http://www.genealogie.com/cgi-bin/fo/afficher.cgi?i> (copy filed 29-12).
2 CONT A monument at Quebec City to LOUIS HEBERT has a plaque on the backside listing JACQUES LE NEUF and his spouse, MARGUERITE LEGARDEUR, among others, as settlers of Quebec City in 1636.  This info gathered from the internet and is fi
2 CONC led L-16-10.
2 CONT Database of Gilles C. Paquette from the internet (filed 29-13).
2 CONT 1666 Census of Trois-Rivieres (the first census taken in Canada) shows Jacques Leneuf, age 60, living with his brother, Michel, age 65.  Jacques' family is listed as follows: wife, Marguerite LeGardeur, age 58. also living with th
2 CONC em are the following domestics: Pierre Millet,71; Pierre Lolat, 23; Laurens Drout, 24; Vincent Marty, 27; Jean Jacques Bourgeois, 17; Jean Bellamy, 18; Estienne Bocart, 25.  Source is filed under censuses.
2 CONT <http://www.genealogie.com/cgi-bin/fo/afficher.cgi?i> (copy filed 29-12) shows the following sources: Jette pg 713; "Memoires de la Societe Genealogique Canadienne Francaise" Vol 51 pg 215; "Dictionnaire Genealogique de nos Origin
2 CONC es"--Denis Beauregard Vol 1 pg 68; "Dictionnaire Biographique du Canada" Vol 1 pg 478.
