1 NAME Joseph /Robineau/
2 GIVN Joseph
2 SURN Robineau
2 _MARNM Robineau de Villebon
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 22 AUG 1655
2 ADDR
3 CITY Québec
3 STAE Colony of Canada
3 CTRY La Nouvelle-France [French Colonial North America]
1 DEAT
2 DATE 5 JUL 1700
2 PLAC Fort Saint-Jean
2 ADDR
3 CITY Saint-Jean-sur-Richelieu
3 STAE Acadie
3 CTRY La Nouvelle-France [French Colonial North America]
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''Sources:'''
2 CONT **https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joseph_Robineau_de_Villebon
2 CONT **https://www.biographi.ca/en/bio/robinau_de_villebon_joseph_1E.html
2 CONT **https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_governors_of_Acadia
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Notes'''
2 CONT **Appointed Governor of Acadie: Successfully assumed command in 1690 following the capture of Port Royal, restoring authority in a chaotic period. (1691–1700)
2 CONT **Established Fort Nashwaak: Rebuilt the seat of government at Fort Nashwaak (1692) farther up the Saint John River, providing a more defensible position against New England.
2 CONT **Defended Against New England: Successfully held the province against multiple English attacks, including defending Fort Nashwaak against a major siege by Benjamin Church in 1696.
2 CONT **Organized Indigenous Alliances: Maintained critical alliances with the Wabanaki Confederacy, utilizing their assistance to protect the Maine-Acadia border region.
2 CONT **Successful Raid on Pemaquid (1696): Coordinated, alongside Pierre Maisonnat and Indigenous allies, the strategic successful siege and destruction of Fort Pemaquid.
2 CONT **Maintained Border Integrity: Successfully maintained the Acadian boundary against New England expansion throughout his tenure, 1690–1700.
2 CONT **Maritime Raid Coordination: Successfully utilized privateers like Pierre Maisonnat (dit Baptiste) to harass English shipping and maintain control of coastal waters.
2 CONT **It appears that Joseph never married. However a certain Marie-Anne Robinau, is considered to be his illegitimate daughter, but there is no proof of this relationship.
2 CONT ----
