1 NOTE {geni:about_me} French nval officer, prospector. As a young naval officer he accompanied James II to Ireland in 1687. By 1692 he was fighting for the French in North America. He accompanied Iberville to both Hudson Bay and to the 
2 CONC Mississippi. He worked the coast of New England for a number of years causing much trounle for shipping in and out of Boston, and thus became a hunted man. He was taken prisoner of the British twicw from the high seas, in 1695 and
2 CONC  1704. He learned good English as a result of being a prisoner in Boston, and on various diplomatic missions. He never achieved a high rank due to his insubordination. In 1713 due to the Treaty of Utrecht, Acadia was given to the 
2 CONC English. Isle St Jean (P.E.I.) and the islands of Cape Breton (renamed ile Royale) were retained by the French. He was instrumental in the selection and setup of Louisbourg and Port Toulouse. He was sent west to become Commandant 
2 CONC of Fort La Pointe de Chequamegon, Madeleine Island, Wisconsin im1727, he learned of the Lake superior copper mines, and in 1733 received permission to work them.He operated the first sailing vessel on Lake superior and built up th
2 CONC e settlement at La Pointe in 1739.His mining hopes for the promising copper deposits were dashed by the outbreak of the Sioux-Chippewa war in 1740. Thus ended his hopes for one of the first mining companies in North America.
