2 CONT "Thunder Bay Museum: 'La Ronde Family fonds: Documents relating to Charles Francois Denis de la Ronde, 1763-1840, including a transcript of his will (1840), birth and baptism records (1763), and other legal papers. Also includes M
2 CONC rs. Schneider's notes relating to the Laronde house in Penetanguishene." [7]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT 22 June 1818 After the publication of three banns, marriage of Charles Francois Delaronde Thibaudiere, squire and voyageur and Magdeleine Pemadjiwanoke, an Indian of Lac de la Clie, in this mission at the present. Present at the s
2 CONC ervice were: Pierre Gamelin Gaucher, Antoine Hyacinthe Lemaire St. Germaine, Toussaint Pilot and Francoist Langevin dit Lacroix. Nine chidren were born before the couple were married: Michel Antoine age 20 yrs., 4 mos.; Marie Loui
2 CONC se bn. 25 Sept. 1800; Marie Anne Angelique bn. 1 Nov. 1804; Julie bn. 23 Jun. 1807, Elizabeth Agathe bn. 17 Dec. 1808; Elizabeth bn. 27 Jan. 1811; Paul bn. 29 Apr. 1813, Etienne bn. 24 Jun.1815 and Marquerite bn.8 Jun. 1817 are re
2 CONC cognized as their legitmate issue by the ceremony. Now, it states in the entry above that there were 9 children born to this couple; however, a close examination of the few pages prior of page 305 and it reveals evidence that ther
2 CONC e were more likely 10 children.
2 CONT
2 CONT La Ronde, Charles, a titled gentleman who claimed descent from the Bourbons of France. Letters addressed to him always bore his title. One of his ancestors was Sieur Pierre Denys de la Ronde, who obtained a grant in the city of Qu
2 CONC ebec in 1658. Charles lived at Penetanguishene, Beausoleil Island and Coldwater. - This paragraph is copied from the book "Migration of the voyageurs from Drummond Island ti Penetanguishene 1828"
