1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Drafted the Cedula of Population with King Charles III of Spain in 1783 that legally and financially endorsed the migration to Trinidad of white and free persons of colour (and their accompanying slaves) of the Rom
2 CONC an Catholic faith without regard to nationality, significantly increasing the resident population over the subsequent 14 years, and effectively transforming Trinidad into a plantation economy in the French Creole dominant style.
2 CONT Grenada born; after living in Trinidad as well as Tobago (where he met his second wife) for some time, he subsequently went to Haiti on assignment, befriended Toussaint L'Ouverture, who acted as witness to his second marriage, bef
2 CONC ore eventually moving to Paris, where he died soon after.
