1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Biography'''
2 CONT Louis was born in 1765. He passed away in 1806.
2 CONT
2 CONT Went by the name Joseph La Framboise. Son of Jean Baptiste Fafard dit La Framboise and Margerite La Bissoniere. Joseph was a very successful fur trader in the Michigan area of the Northwest Territory. Operated several trading post
2 CONC s including at Gabagouache (present day Grand Haven, MI) and in the now Ada/Lowell area of Michigan.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Marguerite Magdeline Marcot, by Indian ceremony, in 1794. They would have the marriage solemnized by a Catholic priest on July 1, 1804 at St. Anne's de Michilimackinac Church on Mackinac Island. The couple would have two c
2 CONC hildren (Josette and Joseph).
2 CONT
2 CONT While traveling to their winter post near Ada/Lowell, MI, Joseph and his wife made their last encampment near Gabagouache. That evening, while praying on his knees, Joseph was shot to death by an enraged Indian who Joseph had refu
2 CONC sed to sell alcohol to earlier in the day. Magdeline continued on to Gabagouache and buried her husband there. She would then continue on to the winter post where she very successfully continued their trading business until her pe
2 CONC rmanent return to Mackinac Island in 1818.
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis Joseph La Framboise was known to be firm, determined, very fair in his business dealings and a very devout Catholic man.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sources'''
2 CONT Find a Grave, database and images (https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/128290227/louis_joseph-la_framboise: accessed October 9, 2024), memorial page for Louis Joseph La Framboise (6 May 1765–Sep 1806), Find a Grave Memorial ID 128
2 CONC 290227; Burial Details Unknown; Maintained by Phil Montroy (contributor 48401446).
2 CONT Family Tree of Louis Laframboise @ https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Laframboise-520
2 CONT
