1 NAME Théophile Onesime /Rivard/
2 GIVN Théophile Onesime
2 _MARNM Rivard
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 ADDR
3 ADR1 141 Church Hill Road
3 CITY Somerset
3 STAE Wisconsin
3 POST 54025
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE 13 APR 1835
1 DEAT
2 DATE 12 MAY 1913
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Theophile O. Rivard, for some years a farmer in Sommerset Townsship, Polk County, Wisconsin, not far from Turtle Lake, Wisconsin, was born in Canada of French ancestry. He came to the United States in 1855 and loca
2 CONC ted in St. Paul. He was a carpenter by trade and assisted in the construction of many buildings in that city. From St. Paul he went to Chippewa Falls, Wisconsin, and thence to Menomonie, Wisconsin. Then he settled in Sommerset Tow
2 CONC nship, where he farmed until his death in 1913.
2 CONT
2 CONT Theo was married at Menomonie to Mary Lamire, whose parents were early settlers of St. Croix County, Wisconsin, where she had spent most of her life. They were the parents of twelve children of whom eight survived infancy: Fred, w
2 CONC ho lived in Minneapolis: Adelaide, wife of John Parnell, of Sommerset Township; Eugene, a business man in Sommerset Township; Samuel, who lived on the home farm in Sommerset Township; Mary, widow of Andrew Campeau and who lived in
2 CONC  Sommerset Township; John, was a traveling salesman who lived in Portland, Oregon; Margaret became a nun and took the name of Sister Mary Reita and lived in a convent at Concordia, Kansas; and Louis H., lived in Turtle Lake, Wisco
2 CONC nsin.
2 CONT
2 CONT Abstracted from pages 156/157 of the History Of Barron County, Wisconsin, published in 1922 by H.C. Cooper, Jr. & Co., Minneapolis, Minnesota.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thanks to John Christeson (#46562435) for the contribution.
