1 NOTE 1880 fed. census; Chesterfield, Essex, NY; 80 y.o. laborer; he and parents born in Canada; listed in Ancestry.com as "Francis Glodza" and wife "Victoria" (95?)Starting with the 1840 U.S. census we find the first of numerous misspe
2 CONC llings of "Gladu" - probably due to their heavy French-Canadian accent and their illiteracy. Three brothers, sons of Basile Gladu-Sanschagrin of Marieville (born about 1788), came to Keeseville, NY in the late 1830's to find jobs.
2 CONC  Peter, Joseph and Francis (Pierre, Joseph and Francois Gladu) were probably among the first Gladu to come south to Keeseville, NY. Other brothers (including Jerry/Jeremie and Thomas/Domase) and other relatives would follow. In th
2 CONC e 1840 census for Keeseville, the Gladu brothers name was spelled "Glaudieu".
2 CONT
2 CONT 1840 fed. census; Ausable, Clinton, NY; p.320; "Francis Glaudieu" (same page as "Joseph & Peter Glaudieu"); heads of household only; all facts fit for this Francis: he is 20-30, wife is 30-40, & they have one child -- a boy under 
2 CONC 5 y.o.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1850 fed. census; Ausable, Clinton, NY; 36 y.o. laborer; listed as "Francis Gludou"; same page as Gladwa and Gladgo
2 CONT 1850 census: Francis Gladwa; 36; wife Victorry, 41; children: Modeste 12, Matthew 8, Julia 5
2 CONT
2 CONT 1860 fed. census; (Keeseville) Ausable, Clinton, NY: p.56 of 84; listed as "Francis Gaudo"; 40 y.o.; illiterate; nailer
2 CONT
2 CONT 1870 fed. census; Keeseville, Clinton, NY; "Francis Goddu" and wife are illiterate; both born in Canada
2 CONT
2 CONT [see RIN 194, 427, 1284]
2 CONT
2 CONT gravestone: "France Gladu; Décédé Le 25 Nov 1896  A l'ae de 84 Ans."
