1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Joseph Francois Laframboise'''
2 CONT '''Born''' 29 Jul 1776 in Mackinac Island, Mackinac, Michigan Territory, United States 
2 CONT '''Died''' 1848 at about age 71 in St. Boniface, Red River Settlement, Rupert's Land
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Joseph Francois Laframboise'''
2 CONT '''Son''' of Alexis (La Framboise) LaFramboise and Marguerite (Sauragess Sauteuse) Saulteaux
2 CONT '''Brother''' of Alexis Laframboise [half]
2 CONT '''Husband''' of Josephte (Assiniboine) Laframboise — married 1799 in St. François Xavier, Red River Settlement, Rupert's Land
2 CONT '''Father''' of Joseph Laframboise, Marguerite (Laframboise) Dumont, Jean Baptiste Laframboise and Louise Laframboise 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Biography'''
2 CONT Father Alexis FAFARD DIT LAFRAMBOISE b: BET 1758 AND 1762
2 CONT Mother Marguerite SAULTEAUX b: BET 1746 AND 1766
2 CONT Marriage 1
2 CONT Marriage 2 Josephte ASSINIBOINE INDIAN WOMAN b: BET 1776 AND 1785.Married: BET 1794 AND 1804
2 CONT Joseph, Leblanc Laframboise Sr. was born 29 July 1776 on Mackinac Island, Michigan, and died 1848. He married Josephte Sha-we-na-quah, Assiniboine, born about 1780. They were married about 1799, in Parish of St. François Xavier. M
2 CONC anitoba. The areas where the family lived were Pembina, North Dakota; Little Rock, Minnesota; Mackinac Island, Michigan and the Red River Settlement
2 CONT Children
2 CONT Joseph Fafard LeBlanc dit Fafard dit LaFramboise Jr b: 1790 in Michillimackinac, Mackinac Cty., MI
2 CONT Augustin LaFramboise b: ABT 1795
2 CONT Marguerite LaFramboise b: 1805 in Red River Settlement, Manitoba, Canada
2 CONT Jean Baptiste LaFramboise b: 1806 in Northwest Territory, Canada
2 CONT LaLouise or Louise LaFramboise b: 1807
2 CONT St Pierre LaFramboise b: ABT 1811
2 CONT Francois LaFramboise b: 1 Nov 1827 in Edmonton, Canada
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Research Notes'''
2 CONT Joseph LaFRAMBOISE b. 29 July 1776,[1] at Michillimackinac (Mackinac Island), Mackinac County, Michigan. m. (1) Veronique _____, b. 1795, m. (2) Josephte ASSINBOIN, m. (3) c. 1822, Marie-Cecile DUMONT, b. 1800.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph died c.1879. [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Email- from: Mare Boelter to Lesage, Wed. 28 Apr 1999 subject: "Re:Metis." Ref: Metis Families; A Genealogical Compendium by Gail Morin.
2 CONT
2 CONT However this cannot be as Joseph was bp. 1796 not 1776 as stated by Morin, so marriage & children must be by a different Joseph. Marie-Cecile: Ref: email from Serena Willis to Mare Boelter 29 Apr 1999, Subject:"Re:Martell";
2 CONT
2 CONT Three generations named Joseph Laframboise appear to be conflated in available online genealogies. The elder, born 1770-1777, married (c. 1799) Sha-we-na-qua/ Josephte ‘L’Assiniboine’ (born c. 1778), and died 1848 (St. Boniface); 
2 CONC his son Joseph ‘Leblanc’, born 1800/ 1806, married Marie Cecile Dumont/ Dumond (daughter of Jean Dumont/ Dumond and Susette ‘Sarcee’; previously married to Joseph Desmarais and Jacques Berger); his son Joseph Narcisse Laframboise 
2 CONC was born 1828 (brother to Jean Baptiste above).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sources'''
2 CONT 1. ↑ "Laframboise, Joseph Sr (b. 1776)" by Lawrence J. Barkwell, Louis Riel Institute.
2 CONT 2. ↑ Veronique: Menominee. Info from Wisconsin's Early French Habitants by J.B. Alderson & K.A. Rennert. Josephte:
2 CONT -https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/LRWT-VYR
2 CONT -UWW [1]
2 CONT -Wordpress [2]
2 CONT -Title: Metis Families, A Genealogical Compendium.Author: Gail Morin, Publication: Quinton Publications, Pawtucket, Rhode Island 1996(fact imported into family tree by Tom Edworthy) Repository: Media: Book Page: v1-326, v1-377, 1-
2 CONC 324, v1-60
2 CONT -Title: Metis Families, A Genealogical Compendium by Gail Morin.Author: Gail Morin, Publication: published by Quintin publications, Pawtucket, Rhode Island-Copyright 2000, fact imported by Tom Edworthy Note: previous version publi
2 CONC shed 1996 Repository: Media: Book Page: v1-116
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source:''' WikiTree contributors, "Joseph Francois Laframboise (1776-1848)," WikiTree: The Free Family Tree, (https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Laframboise-152 : accessed 25 June 2025).
2 CONT .....
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Laframboise, Joseph Sr. (1776-1848)'''
2 CONT Joseph, Laframboise Sr. was born 29 July 1776 on Mackinac Island, Michigan, and died 1848. He married Josephte Sha-we-na-quah, Assiniboine, born about 1780. They were married about 1799, in Parish of St. François Xavier. Manitoba.
2 CONC  The areas where the family lived were Pembina, North Dakota; Little Rock, Minnesota; Mackinac Island, Michigan and the Red River Settlement.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their son Joseph Laframboise Jr. (dit Fafard, aka Leblanc), was born in 1790 on Mackinac Island, Michigan. He married Marie Cecil Dumont, born about 1800.23 She was the daughter of Jean Baptiste Dumont Jr., also known as Ekapow, a
2 CONC  French Voyageur, was born circa 1770 in Montreal, Quebec. In addition to being an HBC employee he was a hunter, trapper, and trader on the Saskatchewan River. He married Josette (Susette) Sarcee born ca. 1770. She was of Sarcee a
2 CONC nd Crow descent. Their son, Isidore Dumont, born ca. 1800 married Louise Laframboise, born 1807. Her background was French / Saulteau / Ojibwa / Assiniboine. She was the daughter of Joseph Laframboise Sr., French / Saulteau / Ojib
2 CONC wa / Assinaboine, and Josephte, an Assiniboine woman. Louise and Isidore were the parents of Gabriel Dumont, born 1837 in St. Boniface, Red River. Gabriel’s father Isidore had a sister, Marie-Cecil Dumont - and she married Joseph 
2 CONC Laframboise Jr., the brother of Louise Laframboise (who married Isidore Dumont). They were brother and sister of one family marrying another brother and sister.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source:'''  Barkwell, Lawrence J., editor. Métis Dictionary of Biography. Louis Riel Institute, [2014]. 
2 CONT .....
