2 CONT
2 CONT Jean-Jacob Heppell was born in 1753 in Salem, New York United States to Nicolas Heppell and Mary Reis. He married Agnes Lavioe on January 19, 1790, and they were married until Agnes' death. They had a child Therese (Heppell). He w
2 CONC ould also marry Victoire Bouillon on April 24, 1798 at St-Germain Rimouski in Rimouski, Bas-Saint-Laurent County, Québec Canada. They had children Joseph Heppell, Jean Heppell, Basile Heppell, and Marie (Heppell). Jean-Jacob Heppe
2 CONC ll died at age 79 years old on April 14, 1833.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: https://www.nosorigines.qc.ca/GenealogieQuebec.aspx?genealogie=Heppell_Jean-Jacob&pid=930
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/en/tree/person/about/MR8F-1Q6
2 CONT Brief Life History of John Jacob
2 CONT
2 CONT When John Jacob Heppell was born on 24 June 1753, in Salem, Salem, Washington, New York, United States, his father, Nicolas Heppell, was 18 and his mother, Marie Reiss, was 14. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married 1st wife Agnes Lavoie circa 1789, in Rimouski, Quebec, Canada. They were the parents of at least 1 son and 3 daughters. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married 2nd wife Victoire Bouillon (1775–1827)
2 CONT on 24 avril 1798 in Rimouski, Rimouski-Neigette, Québec, Canada
2 CONT They had at least 8 children
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 14 April 1833, in Saint-Germain, Rimouski, Rimouski-Neigette, Quebec, Canada, at the age of 79.
