1 NOTE Allen Fleury
2 CONT
2 CONT Residence Isle La Motte VT;
2 CONT Enlisted on 7/28/1862 as a Private.
2 CONT On 9/1/1862 he mustered into "K" Co. VT 1st Heavy Artillery
2 CONT He was Mustered Out on 5/23/1865
2 CONT He was listed as:
2 CONT POW 6/23/1864 Weldon Railroad, VA
2 CONT Paroled 4/28/1865 (place not stated)
2 CONT Promotions:
2 CONT Corpl 1/31/1864
2 CONT Sergt 10/25/1864
2 CONT
2 CONT Additional Information:
2 CONT Allen Scott Fleury  Released at Baldwin, Florida and paroled 4/28/65  at Jacksonville, Florida. Reported Camp Parole, Maryland, 5/11/65. Mustered out 5/23/65.  Sent to Augusta, Maine, 5/30/65. Residing in St. Albans, Vermont, on t
2 CONC he SFVHA 1890 Roster. He lived variously in South Barre, Vermont; Burke, New York; and Isle LaMotte working as a teacher, a clerk in a sash & blinds factory, a deputy collector in the Customs Service for 12 years stationed at St. 
2 CONC Albans and Swanton; and finally employed in the General Freight Department of the Central Vermont Railroad at St. Albans.  Vermont Governor J. A. Mead appointed him a state inspector of weights and measure in 1911.  Died 8/25/1912
2 CONC  of carcinoma of prostate, cystitis, and interstitial nephritis. Buried in the Riverside Cemetery at  Swanton, Vermont. His gravestone bears the weathered inscription:
2 CONT
2 CONT H. ART. CO. K 11th VT. VOL
2 CONT
2 CONT  Granted a disability pension in 1865 of $4 per month on account of diarrhea, scurvy, disease of chest, and of rheumatism which was increased from time to time…to $72 at the time of his death.  Belle S. Fleury granted a widow's pe
2 CONC nsion in 1912. Also listed as Allen S. Flenry at Andersonville.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources: http://www.weldonrailroad.com/updates.html
2 CONT http://www.civilwardata.com/active/hdsquery.dll?SoldierHistory?U&651890
