1 NAME Antoine /Cottenoir/
2 GIVN Antoine
2 SURN Cottenoir
2 _MARNM Cotnoir
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Precious Blood Cemetery
2 ADDR
3 CITY Woonsocket
3 STAE Rhode Island
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE 13 MAY 1852
2 ADDR
3 CITY Saint-David
3 STAE QC
3 CTRY Canada
1 DEAT
2 DATE 11 DEC 1939
2 ADDR
3 CITY Woonsocket
3 STAE Rhode Island
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU Farmer
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Antoine Cotnoir''' (baptised: Quotenoire)
2 CONT
2 CONT Born: 13 May 1852; baptized: 16th at St. David, Yamaska, PQ s/o Joseph Quotenoire & Marie Esther Gasselin dite St. Germain
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: 17 August 1875 at St Cyrille-de-Wendover, Drummond, PQ to Vitaline Tancrell/Tancrede, d/o Euleisippe Tancrell/Tancrede & Zoé Theroux/Heroux
2 CONT
2 CONT Immigration: Immigration to United States 1888
2 CONT
2 CONT Died: 11 December 1939 in Woonsocket, RI, USA (WRI); buried: Precious Blood Cemetery (PBC), Rathbun St. WRI
2 CONT
2 CONT Variants: Cotnoir: Cottenoir(e), Cotte-Noir, Quotenoire Gasselin: Gosselin, Gaisin, Gaussain, Gaucin, St. Germain Tancrell: Tancrede, Tancre, Tancrelle Antoine: Antonio Vitaline: Victorine
2 CONT
2 CONT Antoine was a “cultivateur” (farmer) when he lived in Québec.
2 CONT
2 CONT Per the 1910 WRI census: Vitaline, Damase, & Artémise emigrated to the US in 1888. Antoine came ahead of them in 1865 as well as David in 1884. In 1910 Antoine was working as a wood chopper, David as a polisher in a machine shop, 
2 CONC Damase as a laborer at odd jobs, Artémise as a spinner in a woolen mill, and Emile as a laborer in a woolen mill, and mémère (“Rosanna” in the census) was still at home with her mom.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Marie Délia Cotte-Noir “Délia” Born/baptised: 25 June 1876 St Cyrille-de-Wendover, Drummond, PQ Married: 16 January 1899 at St. Louis, Bonsecoeurs, Richelieu, PQ to Jean-Baptiste Larochelle Died:
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Marie Clara Cotte-Noir “Clara” Born/baptised: 19 February 1878 St Cyrille-de-Wendover, Drummond, PQ Married: to Joseph Lataille Died:
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. David Cotte-Noir Born/baptised: 1 April 1879 St Cyrille-de-Wendover, Drummond, PQ Married: 16 April 1917 at Precious Blood Church, WRI to Josephine Lapointe Died: 11 January 1950 in WRI buried: PBC
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Marie Louise Cotte-Noir Born/baptised: 24 May 1880 St Cyrille-de-Wendover, Drummond, PQ Married: Died:
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Damase Cotnoir (aka “Louis” Damase Cotnoir)* Born/baptised: 18 September 1880 St Cyrille-de-Wendover, Drummond, PQ Married: to Eva E. Glaude d/o Delphis Glaude & Celina Leclair Died: 27 November 1960 res: WRI d: Providence,RI b
2 CONC ur: St. Charles Cemetery, Farm St., Blackstone, MA
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Ignace Elie Cotnoir Born/baptised: 1 February 1883 St Cyrille-de-Wendover, Drummond, PQ Died: 4 February 1883 St Cyrille-de-Wendover, Drummond, PQ
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. Marie Emélie Cotnoir Born/baptised: 21 June 1884 St Cyrille-de-Wendover, Drummond, PQ Died: 21 August 1884 St Cyrille-de-Wendover, Drummond, PQ
2 CONT
2 CONT 8. Joseph Eulycippe Cotnoir Born/baptised: 9 August 1885 St Cyrille-de-Wendover, Drummond, PQ Married: 10 June 1907 at PB Church, WRI to Marie-Ann Paradis Died: 1965 bur: St. John’s Cemetery, N. Smithfield,RI
2 CONT
2 CONT 9. Marie Emélie Artémise Cotnoir “Mise” Born/baptised: 5 January 1877 St Cyrille-de-Wendover, Drummond, PQ Married: to Henri Anger Died:
2 CONT
2 CONT 10. Alfred Cotnoir Born: 14 August 1888 baptised: 16th at PB Church, WRI Godparents: Alfred Tancrede & Geneviève Tancrede Died:
2 CONT
2 CONT 11. Georgiana Cottenoir Born: 16 October 1889 baptised: 17th at PB Church, WRI Godparents: Joseph Tancrede & Georgiana Auger Died:
2 CONT
2 CONT 12. Marie Emélie Cotnoir Born: 26 August 1891 baptised: 27th at PB Church, WRI Godparents: Noemus Cratte & Délia Cotnoir Married: to Victor Lavimodière Died:
2 CONT
2 CONT 13. Joseph Emile Antoine Cotnoir (Sr.) “Emile” Born: 12 December 1892 baptised: 15th at PB Church, WRI Godparents: Delphis Tancrede & ? Tancrede Married: to Anna C. Marks Died: 7 November 1975 bur: St. Charles Cemetery, Farm St., 
2 CONC Blackstone, MA
2 CONT
2 CONT 14. Alfred Cotnoir Born: 18 July1894 baptised: 19th at PB Church, WRI Godparents: David Cotnoir & Clara Cotnoir Died:
2 CONT
2 CONT 15. Marie-Jeanne Cottenoir “Rose”** Born: 5 August 1895 on Sayles Ave., WRI baptised: 8th at PB Church, WRI Godparents: Delphis tancrede & ? Tancrede Married: 15 November 1915 to Henri Gentès s/o Henri Gentès, Sr. & Marie Tourigny
2 CONC  (dite Deshaies) Died: 7 September 1994 L’Hospice St. Antoine, N. Smithfield, RI bur: Cemetery, Farm St., Blackstone, MA
2 CONT
2 CONT *He was an alcoholic. The women would all have to hide their perfume when he came over because he’d even drink that!
2 CONT
2 CONT **According to “the ma tauntes” (Ma Taunte Rita & Ma Taunte Lucille), everyone in the family always called Marie-Jeanne “Rose”. Her sister-in-law, Anna (Marks) w/o Emile, was the only one who used to call her “Rosanna”.
